{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Send one from among you, etc.</b> Yet they did not do so, for they feared the distress of their father over all of them." "<b>Further,</b> they knew with certainty that he would not send Benjamin — and go out and learn how much effort all of them together exerted until they sent him, with the argument that Judah would guarantee and he would bring him. For if Judah and all his brothers were in prison, what confidence would Jacob have to send Benjamin, and the guarantor needs to get him out of confinement?" "<b>Or,</b> they never had any intention of separating under any circumstances, for they were afraid of separation lest one be held accountable for being alone. In the end they did not agree to leave one of them behind, except because the test was contingent upon this for them, as I shall explain in the verse (Genesis 42:19): ״אִם כֵּנִים וְגוֹ׳ וְלֹא תָמוּתוּ״ — then they were compelled by their own actions."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:01.289611664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}